      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "to identify features of lipid profile in women with rheumatoid arthritis (RA) depending on calcification of coronary arteries (CA)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "We examined 40 women with RA (mean age 48.6 ± 1.4 years, average duration of RA 7.77 ± 1 years) and 22 women of control group. Coronary artery calcification was detected by multislice computed tomography and expressed as Agatston score."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Frequency and degree of CA calcification in patients with RA was comparable with those in control group (=0.163 and =0.734, respectively). Calcification of CA in RA patients was accompanied by elevated levels of total and low density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol, non-high density lipoprotein cholesterol, LDL, and atherogeneity index. In all patients with CA calcification LDL cholesterol level exceeded 2.5 mmol/l."
        }
      ]},
